Extract ONLY locations and areas from the adventure.

STRICT RULES:
- JSON ONLY
- Do not include NPCs, items, encounters, or plot logic
- Areas must belong to locations
- Use stable area IDs (e.g. "1A", "2C", "CAVE_ENTRANCE")

Return EXACTLY this structure:

ID RULES (MANDATORY):
- All IDs must be lowercase ASCII
- Format: <entity>.<slug>[.<context>]
- Slugs use underscores only
- IDs must be stable and deterministic
- If a collision occurs, append .2, .3, etc
- Never reuse an ID for a different entity

{
  "locations": [
    {
      "id": "string",
      "name": "string",
      "description": "short neutral description"
    }
  ],
  "areas": [
    {
      "id": "string",
      "location_id": "string",
      "name": "string",
      "description": "player-facing description",
      "connects_to": ["area_id"],
      "features": ["string"],
      "hazards": ["string"]
    }
  ]
}

If a field is not described in the text, use an empty array.
